{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487598-trying-to-work-out-a-alagam-discipline","id":1487598,"title":"Trying to work out a Alagam discipline.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-23T09:06:29-07:00","id":1487598,"title":"Trying to work out a Alagam discipline.","content":"This idea was inspired by a high level Dominate discipline that I read in Guide To The Camarilla. Instead of mentally manipulating one childer, grand-childer and so on to act on your wishes. This is is more passive intelligence gathering and keeping tabs on a particular lineage.<br /> <br /> So here goes. The working title is See Through The Blood<br /> <br /> I figure it would be a level 4 or 5 Auspex power but I'm unsure If I should use a Blood Sorcery ritual or Obuscate powers. I want it it to be very subtle and passive that you don't know that your Great Great Great Grandsire is tracking you or using your senses to get a better picture of what is happening.<br /> <br /> I think that it should be at least two Rouse points or do you think it should somewhat higher? I'm stuck on the dice pool to use I know Auspex is needed but should I use Insight, Awareness or Investigation in the dice pool and I'm trying to work on a limitation on this abilty. For example a 4th generation Kindred would get excellent quality information from there direct childer and grand-childer. Then it weakens as the generation gap gets wider and wider.<br /> <br /> I would welcome any ideas to help improve on this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T19:37:46-07:00","id":1487675,"title":"","content":"Do you mean &quot;amalgam discipline&quot;/combo/devotion?<br /> <br /> Not wanting to be a grammar nazi or anything, but Alagam confused the hell out of me for the whole day, even after i did read your post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of the power per se, honestly Auspex+Blood Sorcery seems like the better fit to me, considering Path of Blood is the one that possesses powers relating to extracting knowledge and manipulating vitae one's own or another's. That said i'll be the first to admit i'm not all that versed in how the disciplines are arranged in V5, being more of a &quot;2nd to V20&quot; kind of guy, so to speak (though i do have some experience playing &amp; STing with Requiem too).<br /> <br /> As an aside, don't know how things are in that specific arena in V5, but i'm pretty sure 3 discipline combinationos were possible in Requiem though far from uncommon and kind of stretching limits, so Auspex + Blood Magic + Obfuscate might be a viable technique if one wants to go there, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-23-2022, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T19:47:37-07:00","id":1487677,"title":"","content":"in V5:<br /> Information Gathering = Auspex.<br /> Subtle/Unnoticeable due to mind &quot;obfuscation&quot; = Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> (Dominate &lt;never&gt; gathers info in V5).<br /> <br /> V5 Auspex 3 &quot;Share the Senses&quot; already does that; the limit is &quot;someone that still have your Blood in their body&quot;.<br /> To use Obfuscate remotely, the smallest level in core book is 3 (Ghost in the Machine), so, I'd use this as the base level.<br /> <br /> So, the final power would be = &quot;Share the Senses&quot;, but with the added characteristics of: + can be used in any descendant (even if they don't actually have your Blood currently in their system) + can only be noticed if the character is actively looking for it &lt;AND&gt; has &quot;Sense the Unseen&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> my text would be: <hr /><i><b>Scry Through the Blood - Auspex 3; Amalgam: Obfuscate 3</b></i><br /> <i><b>Cost, Dice pool, Duration</b></i>: same as &quot;Share the Senses&quot; (Auspex 3), V5 p.250.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Description</b></i>: same as &quot;Share the Senses&quot; (Auspex 3), V5 p.250, add the following paragraph:<br /> <i>The user may also choose to tap any descendant (Childer, Grand-Childer, and so on); these always count as &quot;someone who still has some of the user\u2019s Blood in their body.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>System</b></i>: same as &quot;Share the Senses&quot; (Auspex 3), V5 p.250., but add the following paragraph just after &quot;(...) Blood that remains in the target.&quot;:<br /> <br /> <i>If the target is a descendant, the Difficulty is 1 for each step of Generation (1 for Childer, 2 for Grand-Childer and so on).</i><br /> <br /> Substitute &quot;The target usually remains unaware of the intrusion, but Sense the Unseen can allow the passenger to be noticed.&quot;<br /> <br /> by <i>&quot;The target remains unaware of the intrusion, but Sense the Unseen can allow the passenger to be noticed - if, and only if - the target knows that this power exists and is actively looking for its use on themselves.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> (maintain the rest of the text as it is in v5).<br /> That would be my version 1.0 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr />Probably most suited to Malkavian Elders and Methuselahs, which I think is perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T04:31:07-07:00","id":1487720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487598-trying-to-work-out-a-alagam-discipline?p=1487677#post1487677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in V5:<br /> Information Gathering = Auspex.<br /> Subtle/Unnoticeable due to mind &quot;obfuscation&quot; = Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> (Dominate gathers info in V5).<br /> <br /> V5 Auspex 3 &quot;Share the Senses&quot; already does that; the limit is &quot;someone that still have your Blood in their body&quot;.<br /> To use Obfuscate remotely, the smallest level in core book is 3 (Ghost in the Machine), so, I'd use this as the base level.<br /> <br /> So, the final power would be = &quot;Share the Senses&quot;, but with the added characteristics of: + can be used in any descendant (even if they don't actually have your Blood currently in their system) + can only be noticed if the character is actively looking for it has &quot;Sense the Unseen&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> my text would be: <hr /><i><b>Scry Through the Blood - Auspex 3; Amalgam: Obfuscate 3</b></i><br /> <i><b>Cost, Dice pool, Duration</b></i>: same as &quot;Share the Senses&quot; (Auspex 3), V5 p.250.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Description</b></i>: same as &quot;Share the Senses&quot; (Auspex 3), V5 p.250, add the following paragraph:<br /> <i>The user may also choose to tap any descendant (Childer, Grand-Childer, and so on); these always count as &quot;someone who still has some of the user\u2019s Blood in their body.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>System</b></i>: same as &quot;Share the Senses&quot; (Auspex 3), V5 p.250., but add the following paragraph just after &quot;(...) Blood that remains in the target.&quot;:<br /> <br /> <i>If the target is a descendant, the Difficulty is 1 for each step of Generation (1 for Childer, 2 for Grand-Childer and so on).</i><br /> <br /> Substitute &quot;The target usually remains unaware of the intrusion, but Sense the Unseen can allow the passenger to be noticed.&quot;<br /> <br /> by <i>&quot;The target remains unaware of the intrusion, but Sense the Unseen can allow the passenger to be noticed - if, and only if - the target knows that this power exists and is actively looking for its use on themselves.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> (maintain the rest of the text as it is in v5).<br /> That would be my version 1.0 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr />Probably most suited to Malkavian Elders and Methuselahs, which I think is perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is too cheap and overpowered for what the OP is proposing. Bear in mind Share the Senses is Difficulty 3.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend increasing the Auspex requirement by at least one, since it partially obviates the drawbacks of Share the Senses. For Auspex 3 and Obfuscate 3, I'd simply say you can use Share the Senses without detection (barring Sense the Unseen), not that you can apply the power to any descendants remotely.<br /> <br /> To operate over a distance, with a much looser and more impersonal connection to the target (you needn't ever have met them, so long as they are of your blood), seems like a significant enough step up in power to warrant Auspex 4 (maybe even 5).<br /> <br /> Balancing this, the people you can target will be relatively few unless you're a Methuselah. But it's still very powerful.<br /> <br /> Here's what I'd go for:<br /> <br /> Blood Sympathy (Auspex 4)<br /> Prerequisite: Share the Senses<br /> Your ability to sense others now extends through your lineage itself. You can use Share the Senses on anyone who shares your clan or bloodline, as if they had your vitae in their body, provided you know their name or face.<br /> Amalgam: Obfuscate 3<br /> Cost: Two rouse checks<br /> Dice pools: Resolve + Auspex<br /> System: Roll Resolve + Auspex at Difficulty 3 to target a close relative, such as a childe or sire, as per Share the Senses. The Difficulty increases by one for every step removed from you the target is. Particularly remote or estranged targets may require a higher Difficulty at the Storyteller's discretion.<br /> Duration: One scene <br /> <br /> Now, this is still slightly different to the OP's suggestion, which was a power that gathers info across a whole bloodline. But it's a start. To do the latter, I'd go slightly differently again:<br /> <br /> Whispers in the Blood (Auspex 5)<br /> Prerequisite: Share the Senses<br /> Across the world, you feel the waxing and waning of your bloodline in subtle sensations, enigmatic dreams and flashes of insight. You feel their approximate numbers and where in the world they have spread, as well as their triumphs and losses, and their relative strength. Such sensations are rarely clear, but you can use this connection to communicate more clearly with effort.<br /> Amalgam: Obfuscate 3<br /> Cost: None<br /> Dice pools: Resolve + Auspex<br /> System: Whenever a close relative, such as a sire or childe, meets Final Death or falls to torpor, you feel it and instinctively know their approximate whereabouts to the nearest city (though you can't tell the difference between Final Death and torpor). For each step away from you, the sensations become weaker and less direct, manifesting as vague images or strange instincts. Strong experiences such as frenzy or intense grief may also send ripples through the Blood, rising for brief moments in your own mind, before settling again. <br /> <br /> Where appropriate, you can attempt to decipher such messages, or gain a rough assessment of your bloodline's welfare as a whole, by rolling Resolve + Auspex. The roll is Difficulty 3 for those one step removed from you (a sire, childe or sibling), and increases by one for every additional step removed from you the subject is, up to a maximum of Difficulty 6 for any member of your bloodline (or to sense the bloodline as a whole). If attempting to learn the welfare of your bloodline, you receive impressions that tell you whether your lineage has suffered great loss or has swelled in ranks, how far around the world they have spread, as well as any hot or cold spots.<br /> <br /> These two Amalgams are based on VTR's Blood Sympathy, to hopefully provide a useful framework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-26-2022, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T09:40:44-07:00","id":1487739,"title":"","content":"I think the Amalgam should be Blood Sorcery, like it's Dominate equivalent, Ancestral Dominion. I think the &quot;spreading your power through the Blood derived from you&quot; is more relevant than the &quot;doing it unnoticed part&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T13:35:59-07:00","id":1487933,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback I appreaciate some of the good ideas that were mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T00:17:33-07:00","id":1487985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487598-trying-to-work-out-a-alagam-discipline?p=1487739#post1487739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Amalgam should be Blood Sorcery, like it's Dominate equivalent, Ancestral Dominion. I think the &amp;quot;spreading your power through the Blood derived from you&amp;quot; is more relevant than the &amp;quot;doing it unnoticed part&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That also works. I guess it depends who you intend the power to be for. Blood Sorcery limits it a little, but that may be what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T12:38:29-07:00","id":1488195,"title":"","content":"Now I have to think of how this power would show up in our game? Most of my friends are playing high generation kindred who max out at the 10th generation and are barely 200 years old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}